1
00:00:00,705 --> 00:00:03,795
(Mrs Koothrappali:)Rajesh, do you remember Lalita Gupta?

2
00:00:03,959 --> 00:00:07,709
(Raj:)The little fat girl that used to kick me
in the samosas and call me untouchable?

3
00:00:07,879 --> 00:00:10,969
(Mrs Koothrappali:)Yes. Well, now she's
a dental student at USC...

4
00:00:11,133 --> 00:00:13,303
(Mrs Koothrappali:)...so we gave her
your contact information.

5
00:00:14,052 --> 00:00:15,092
(Raj:)Why did you do that?

6
00:00:15,262 --> 00:00:17,892
(Dr Koothrappali:)You're 26 years old, Rajesh.
We want grandchildren.

7
00:00:18,056 --> 00:00:21,896
- But, Papa, I'm not supposed...
- Lalita's parents approved the match.

8
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:24,980
(Dr Koothrappali:)If you decide on a spring wedding,
we can avoid monsoon season.

9
00:00:25,147 --> 00:00:26,817
A spring wedding?

10
00:00:26,982 --> 00:00:28,862
It's up to you. We don't want to meddle.

11
00:00:29,025 --> 00:00:31,275
(Raj:)If you don't want to meddle,
why are you meddling?

12
00:00:31,444 --> 00:00:33,534
(Dr Koothrappali:)Your parents
don't consider this meddling.

13
00:00:33,697 --> 00:00:35,947
(Sheldon:)While arranged marriages
are no longer the norm...

14
00:00:36,116 --> 00:00:39,866
(Sheldon:)...Indian parents continue to have
an involvement in their children's love lives.

15
00:00:40,036 --> 00:00:42,746
(Raj:)Why are you telling me
about my own culture?

16
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:44,830
(Sheldon:)You seemed confused.

17
00:00:46,626 --> 00:00:50,626
- Sorry, but with all due respect, I don't...
- I'm sorry, darling. We have to go.

18
00:00:50,797 --> 00:00:52,507
(Mrs Koothrappali:)Doogie Howser is on.

19
00:00:53,425 --> 00:00:55,755
(Mrs Koothrappali:)Grandma, it's Doogie time.

20
00:00:55,927 --> 00:01:01,027
- Bye-bye.
- Bye-bye.

